How MySQL Indexes Work

An index is like a table of contents in a book. Instead of reading the entire book to find a specific topic, you use the table of contents to jump directly to the page.
MySQL uses B-trees or hash tables for storing indexes, depending on the type.
Creating Indexes

1. Creating Index with Table Creation
CREATE TABLE users (
    id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
    name VARCHAR(100),
    email VARCHAR(100),
    INDEX (name) -- Non-unique index
);

2. Adding Index to an Existing Table
CREATE INDEX idx_name ON users (name);

3. Creating a Unique Index
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_email ON users (email);

4. Dropping an Index
DROP INDEX idx_name ON users;

